<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ove Gjedde</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1594">1594</a>–<a href="/years/1660">1660</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ove Gjedde was a Danish naval officer who led the first expedition of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danish-east-india-company">Danish East India Company</a> to Asia, sailing in 1618. After visiting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> he negotiated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raghunatha-nayak">Raghunatha Nayak</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a>, who in 1620 granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> the village of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tharangambadi">Tranquebar</a>, where the fort of Dansborg was built. He later served as Admiral of the Realm.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ove-gjedde.jpg" alt="Ove Gjedde" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karel van Mander III · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karel_van_III_Mander_-_Rigsadmiral_Ove_Gjedde_-_KMS605_-_Statens_Museum_for_Kunst.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A Danish expedition under <b>Ove Gjedde</b> reached south India, and in 1620 Raghunatha Nayak of Thanjavur granted the Danish East India Company the village of Tranquebar (Tharangambadi).</blockquote><a href="/state/danish-india">Danish India</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Tomarps Kungsgård Castle, in what is now <a href="/countries/sweden">Sweden</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copenhagen">Copenhagen</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/denmark">Denmark</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=56.15,13.06&amp;year=1636" aria-label="Tomarps Kungsgård Castle on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4834 252 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Ove Gjedde"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5284 522h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5284 522h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=56.15,13.06&amp;year=1636">What was here in 1636? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
